From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob McSwain <jacob@mcswain.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:10:06 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): a restart hands running turns to the next
 gateway

gateway.restart_turn_handoff (false = off) and restart_turn_handoff_wait_seconds (0): a graceful restart no longer waits for running turns (agent.restart_after_turn_timeout, then the stop's agent.restart_drain_timeout) while every new turn of the profile is refused. After the handoff wait it stops each running turn like a user's Stop and writes the canonical sessions it stopped to $HERMES_HOME/.turn-handoff.json (0600); the gateway that takes the profile over settles a handed-off turn its owner left unknown as interrupted and queues one continuation turn per session in its FIFO. One turn parked on a subagent's approval held a rolling update's restart wait for 406 s, with no chat able to run anything.
